<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net" agent="Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/146.0.0.0 Safari/537.36" version="29.6.3" pages="13">
  <diagram name="Definition GAS" id="a-f_YpFzG5-Z_sWn2wq1">
    <mxGraphModel dx="2316" dy="764" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="827" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="gA4M2xbGnE94rIYVCRG6-1" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;text-align: center; margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;GAS&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;The Gameplay Ability System is a framework for building abilities and interactions that Actors can own and trigger.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;This system is designed mainly for RPGs, action-adventure games, MOBAs, and other types of games where characters have abilities that need to coordinate mechanics, visual effects, animations, sounds, and data-driven elements, although it can be adapted to a wide variety of projects.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;-The Gameplay Ability System also supports replication for multiplayer games, and can save developers a lot of time scaling up their designs to support multiplayer.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fillColor=light-dark(#1BA1E2,#66FFFF);fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#006EAF;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="89" y="40" width="650" height="270" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gA4M2xbGnE94rIYVCRG6-3" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;text-align: center; margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Ingredients&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;- Ability System Component:&amp;nbsp;as a bridge between the Actor and the skill system. The Actor uses or owns this Component to manage Ability, Effect, and Attribute.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;- Attribute Set:&amp;nbsp;Store gameplay values ​​like Health, Mana, Stamina. Attribute Sets are extensible Attribute group containers.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;- Gameplay Ability:&amp;nbsp;Defines the skills or actions that can be triggered by an Actor, which can be attacks, dodges, spells, etc. Can run asynchronously, supporting multi-stage, animation, sound, and network synchronization.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;- Ability Task:&amp;nbsp;Are subtasks for Ability, supporting asynchronous processing such as waiting for animation, playing effects, catching events.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;- Gameplay Effect:&amp;nbsp;Used to change Attribute values ​​or apply state (buff/debuff), according to custom data and logic, can be active/passive, network replication supported.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;- Gameplay Cue:&amp;nbsp;A system dedicated to handling visual effects, sound, and cosmetic graphics feedback, completely separate from the core gameplay logic. It handles visual effects, sound, haptics, lighting, etc. when a Gameplay Effect or Ability is activated.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;- Gameplay Tag:&amp;nbsp;A hierarchical string-based tag system used to mark, classify, and check the state, behavior, or properties of objects in gameplay.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;- Player State:&amp;nbsp;Used to store and manage player state separately and consistently in a multiplayer environment. It will keep state information such as score, life, name, and player characteristic data throughout the game session, even if Pawn is eliminated or renewed (Related to Attribute, Ability System Component).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fillColor=light-dark(#008A00,#00FF00);fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#005700;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-121" y="410" width="1070" height="370" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gA4M2xbGnE94rIYVCRG6-4" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="gA4M2xbGnE94rIYVCRG6-1" target="gA4M2xbGnE94rIYVCRG6-3">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="-200" y="350" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="-150" y="300" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
